From: 77450danik <ddziuba1@stu.vistula.edu.pl>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] shell32: The desktop's icons stay where they are put.

The desktop was always auto-arranged ("Remove LVS_AUTOARRANGE when the view
is able to save ItemPos"): an icon could not be dragged anywhere. As in
Windows 10, Auto arrange is off and Align to grid on by default, and both
are in the desktop's View menu. An icon dropped stays in the nearest cell
of the grid, one dropped over another goes to the nearest free cell, a new
one takes the first free cell, top to bottom and then the next column, and
"Sort by" lays them all out again in that order. Where they are is kept in
the desktop's bag (Bags\1\Desktop, ArcticItemPos) by the items' parsing
names, in thousandths of a cell, so another icon size or scale keeps each in
its cell. A desktop that was auto-arranged before this is once given
Windows' defaults (ArcticFree).
